11
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
South Park: Bigger, Longer & Uncut is a 1999 American adult animated musical
black comedy film based on the animated sitcom South Park.

12
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
The film was directed by series creator Trey Parker, who co-wrote
with series co-creator Matt Stone and Pam Brady.

13
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
It stars Parker, Stone, Mary Kay Bergman, and Isaac Hayes, all of whom reprise their roles from
the series, with George Clooney, Eric Idle, and Mike Judge in supporting roles.

14
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
The plot follows Stan Marsh, Kyle Broflovski, Eric Cartman, and Kenny McCormick as they sneak into an R-rated
film starring the Canadian comedy duo Terrance and Phillip, after which they begin swearing.

15
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
When the consequent moral panic culminates in the United States declaring war on Canada, Stan, Kyle, and Cartman take it upon themselves to save
Terrance and Phillip from execution, while Kenny tries to prevent a prophecy involving Satan and Saddam Hussein's intent to conquer the world.

16
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Primarily centered on themes of censorship and scapegoating, the film also parodies and satirizes the animated films of
the Disney Renaissance, musicals such as Les Misérables, and controversies surrounding the series itself.

17
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
The film also heavily satirizes the Motion Picture Association of America; during production, Parker and Stone disputed with
the MPAA, which returned the film multiple times with an NC-17 rating due to its frequent use of profanity.

18
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
The film's songs were written by Parker and Marc Shaiman,
the latter of whom composed the score.

19
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
South Park: Bigger, Longer & Uncut premiered at Grauman's Chinese Theatre on June 23, 1999, and was released
theatrically in the United States and Canada a week later by Paramount Pictures, with Warner Bros.

20
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
handling international distribution.

21
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
The film received critical acclaim from critics, who praised its
story, voice acting, soundtrack, humor and themes.

22
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Produced on a $21 million budget, it grossed $83.1 million worldwide, making South Park: Bigger, Longer &
Uncut the highest-grossing R-rated animated film until 2016, when it was beaten by Sausage Party.

23
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
At the 72nd Academy Awards, the song "Blame Canada" was nominated for Best Original
Song, but it lost to Phil Collins' "You'll Be in My Heart" from Tarzan.

24
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The film has since been considered one of the
greatest animated films of all time.

25
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
The film explores themes of hell, musical,
surrealism, world supremacy, visions of hell.

26
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
The tone is lighthearted and mind_bending.
